    {
      "id": null,
      "key": "panelPANE-05D333CA8C47D942",
      "title": "",
      "visualSettings": "{\"general\":{\"mode\":\"TextPanel\",\"type\":\"text\",\"displayType\":\"default\"},\"title\":{\"fontSize\":14},\"series\":{},\"text\":{\"format\":\"markdownV2\",\"fontSize\":12,\"showTitle\":false},\"legend\":{\"enabled\":false}}",
      "keepVisualSettingsConsistentWithParent": true,
      "panelType": "TextPanel",
      "text": "#### CPU Load Vs CPU Usage\n - CPU Usage is the percentage of time the CPU is working while CPU Load measures how many programs are using or waiting for a processor core.  \n - How are they different? - You can have a high load with nearly 0% CPU utilization (such as when you have a lot of IO data stuck in a wait state) and you can have a load of 1 and 100% CPU, when you have a single threaded process running full time.\n -  How are they related? - A 4 core CPU with hyperthreading (8 virtual cores) all at 100% for 1 minute would contribute 8 to the 1 minute load average.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": null,
      "key": "panel4FAB7613BDF8084D",
      "title": "",
      "visualSettings": "{\"general\":{\"mode\":\"TextPanel\",\"type\":\"text\",\"displayType\":\"default\"},\"title\":{\"fontSize\":14},\"series\":{},\"legend\":{\"enabled\":false},\"text\":{\"format\":\"markdown\",\"showTitle\":false}}",
      "keepVisualSettingsConsistentWithParent": true,
      "panelType": "TextPanel",
      "text": "### CPU I/O Wait Time\nI/O wait is the percentage of time that CPUs were idle during which the system had pending disk I/O requests.\n\n#### Causes\n* Storage devices that have less throughput are not able to keep up with CPU performance.\n* Unoptimized application code and/or database queries lead to high disk reads/writes.\n* Not having enough free memory leads to swapping and paging to disk."
    }
